      "value": "@{609a1fc2eeec070e82894e8d|full_name}: No, in invite+ people have to send request, but on blue, it will be accepted and you won’t be notified as if it was friends+, than on green as I said, it follows instance types.\n\nGreen and Blue are the same in Public and Friends+ and Friends as these worlds are open anyway to your friends\n\nThey act different in invite and invite+ where on blue, your friends can still join you no matter what (as instance creator for invite ofc) \n\nOrange and Green are different, as said, Green follow instance rule and show Public world you are in; Orange is when you want everything hidden and need peeps to request.\n\nSo no blue is not green, and yes green is working as intended meaning « available following instance type »\n\nWhat you guys ask for is different; from what I get of the original post at least, is to have another status mixing the fact that people need to request all the time like orange, but can see the instance you are in as long as it is public like green\n\nSo like a yellow status\n\nBut green works fine and as it always did and was intended to imo, i like the way things works rn and if I am in private I don’t feel the need that peeps just see the name of the world I am in\n\nBut again just my opinion\n\nI will also add, if you want to be green just for some specific peeps that can join you anytime and don’t want to be joined by others, that is why groups were made",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
