      "value": "@{62def40fd302ec44c0aaec2d|full_name}: Thank you so much for explaining! I genuinely didn't understand because I almost never use anything above Friends+. \n\nI can understand why you like the way things are now but I personally disagree. The vast majority of instances used in VRC, in my experience, are Public and Friends+. If 3/5 instance types (two of them being the most popular) render two status colors the same, they're functionally redundant in those instance types and can be improved upon. Green should act the way it does in Invite and Invite+, just with the addition that you can see the world (which I feel is basically what this post is suggesting if I'm reading it correctly). Private worlds (Invite and Invite+) would still be private, no matter what color you're on.\n\nLocking the functionality of curating who we choose to join us anytime to group-only instances when making them is a VRC+ feature is both clunky and unfair. It's also not the same functionality this is asking for; anyone outside a group can't see where you are. Group instances seem work best for specific purposes (like a D&D group) and large-scale events.\n\nAt the very least, maybe there /should/ be an in-between yellow status.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
