      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It's funny because when I read how the statuses worked, I had assumed that green works like this *already*, but it doesn't. If someone is in Friends, Friends+, or Public, it allows them to auto-join.\n\nI wouldn't mind being on green to show friends where I am, but I also would prefer to have the option to invite, at least if I already can invite people. \n\nFor example, the current functionality of Invite+ is that other users can only invite if they are requested on (I think this is silly, but I digress). It would be helpful to show people that I am in an Invite+ world so they know to request on me.\n\nAnd to recap on that Invite+ thing: I just wish that we were allowed to have more granular control over the instance settings, rather than having these instance types. I really do think Invite+ should be: anyone can invite, but no one can auto-join, since that's what I assumed it should do.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
