        "like": 2
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I wanna add in my two cents. for this.\n\nI am likely one of several people who don't like surprise friend visits the moment I've loaded into VRC, and for me, I like to think of my desire to socialize like an old Windows XP laptop: Slow to boot, but once fully booted, everything runs smoothly until the battery dies.\n\nThat being said, when I'm not \"fully booted,\" I will not be interested in my friends just showing up in my instance and bee-lining straight to me, as that can drain my battery sooner than I'd like.\n\nSo I use Orange. And get no Invites/Requests 'cause Orange might as well be Do Not Disturb.\n\nBut if I use Green, I suddenly have people showing up and instantly wanting to hang out when I've not got the energy just yet, or am even in a map that would be bad for them to join, like Pop Escape [late joiner unfriendly] or No Time Two Talk [unable to se other people until you're matched, and might not be my friend whom I'm matched with].\n\nNot to mention that there was a bug once that made Notifs just fail to show up in game, so even if Sandra Dean or whoever wanted to join me, I could very well just never get the notif 'cause this bug hasn't been fixed/patched out, as far as I'm aware.\n\nYeah, I could also change what my status says, but do people other than me actually read those things often enough to make doing so viable? \n\nLongform short: Orange is too strict for my friends, but Green is too lax for me, and I just want a way that guides people to send Requests/Invites instead of just joining off of me, but also doesn't scare people off from even trying to send any at all, which is what happens given the way things are now.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-25T22:13:22.739Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This change would make the statuses break down very cleanly:\n\n- Show world, auto-accept joins (current blue)\n\n- Show world, curate who joins (my new green)\n\n- Hide world, curate who joins (current orange)\n\n- Hide world, no joins (current red)\n\nHow private you want your hangout to be can change throughout the course of a single conversation. Sometimes you're having a very casual hang and then you get into a serious topic, and might not want people joining during it. Social behavior is fluid and changing status mid-conversation is unnatural and cumbersome.\n\nThis green status change would give a \"door's open, but you still gotta knock\" option, where you're generally open to people joining, but you still want to be able to exercise discretion about who joins and exactly when as the need arises. Orange feels much too private for casual hangouts, but you don't always want ANYBODY to join ALWAYS. Personally if this were implemented, I'd be on it all the time.",
